Friday 21th July 1995

64NET now works with GEOS, however at this stage the drivers must be 
purchased seperately from:

     Performance Peripherals Europe.
     phone: +49 2227 3221

the estimated cost is approx DM25.

* At a later stage the GEOS software for 64net may be bundled with the 64net
distribution, and infact can be purchased at the same time you buy the
registered version of 64net.

TO USE 64NET WITH GEOS:

1) Copy the relevant GEOS files onto your GEOS boot disk, ie:

          64NET CONFIG
          64NET MGR
          64NET MOVE
          64NET TIME
          64NET SET
          64NET PRINT

2) On the IBM-PC run 64NETCFG.EXE from your 64net directory.
   * Ensure that "Virtualised quick-mount list" is active.
   If you have .D64  .D71 or .D81 files you wish to access from GEOS,
   use the "Add Mounts" option to search for them, and assimilate them into
   your mount list.

3) Start 64NET on your IBM-PC

4) Boot your GEOS disk.
   * Run "64NET MGR" from GEOS.  If you have no partitions defined, then 
   create one or more.  This a relatively simple menu driven process.
   * Run "64NET CONFIG" and assign one or more unused drives to be used with 
   64NET.  Then save your configuration and quit.

Once you have followed these steps, GEOS should now recognuise 64NET, and
continue to do so even after re-boot.

NOTE: Do not use RBOOT, as it will not redetect 64NET as the autoexecs will
not necessarily be run



Paul Gardner-Stephen

